# ---- Counted nouns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Slovak plural rule (assets/i18n): one (1) | few (2, 3, 4) | other (0, 5 and more, and every
# compound: 21, 22, 102 ...). Written with digits ("3 ťahy"), spoken with the number word in the noun's
# gender. These are nominative forms, also the accusative of the inanimate masculine and neuter nouns
# ("potrebuješ tri ťahy", "stratil som dva body"). Feminine and animate nouns have accusative keys
# (<noun>_acc: "vzal som ti {n:piece_acc}" = "jednu figúru / dve figúry / päť figúr"). Other cases of
# a counted noun do not exist: rephrase with the nominative or accusative ("Vrátené ťahy: {n:move}").
# A counted noun as the subject changes the verb with the number ("stačí jeden ťah", "stačia dva ťahy",
# "stačí päť ťahov"): keep counted nouns as objects or after a colon.
count.move = {n} ťah|{n} ťahy|{n} ťahov
count.point = {n} bod|{n} body|{n} bodov
count.pawn = {n} pešiak|{n:an} pešiaci|{n} pešiakov
