# ---- Move numbers: ordinals -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A move number is an ordinal, written with its period and spoken as a word, in the case the sentence
# needs: "{n:ord} ťah" = "12. ťah" / "dvanásty ťah" (nominative and accusative), "do {n:ord_gen} ťahu"
# = "do 12. ťahu" / "do dvanásteho ťahu", "k {n:ord_dat} ťahu", "v {n:ord_loc} ťahu" = "v 12. ťahu" /
# "v dvanástom ťahu", "{n:ord_ins} ťahom" = "12. ťahom" / "dvanástym ťahom" ("mat 3. ťahom"). Always
# put the noun ("ťah") right after it: the written period would otherwise end the sentence. Never "s"
# or "z" right before it ("so štvrtým", "zo šiesteho" depend on the number): use v, do, od, po, k.
# Above 20 the voice composes "dvadsať prvom" (= "dvadsaťprvom", the accepted short form of
# "dvadsiatom prvom") and "sto dvadsiatom". 0 is "nultý".
